WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.656
The experiments span synthetic and real data.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:07.392
On the synthetic side,

00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:11.127
the authors build linear and nonlinear functional
targets with either exponential or polynomial

00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:14.863
decaying memory and sweep the hidden dimension from
about two up to sixty four to watch

00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:18.599
how the perturbation-stability radius behaves.

00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:22.335
They also construct randomly initialized RNN
teacher models with a large hidden dimension

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:26.071
of two hundred fifty six and approximate them with
student RNNs to test the stability

00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:29.807
filter.

00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:33.543
On real data,

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:37.278
they query the memory function of LSTM models on
IMDB movie-review sentiment analysis,

00:00:37.358 --> 00:00:41.014
and they train nonlinear RNNs on MNIST image
classification to test the optimization benefits

00:00:41.094 --> 00:00:44.750
of stable reparameterization.
